# Original fictional watershed-monitoring corpus for operational trials.
requirement OPS-MONITOR-001
title: Monitor watershed conditions
statement:
  The monitoring service shall provide current watershed conditions for every deployed station.
rationale:
  Operators need a common operational picture before deciding whether intervention is required.
end requirement

requirement SYS-MONITOR-SAMPLE-001
title: Sample field sensors
statement:
  Each station shall acquire water-level, flow-rate, and precipitation samples at least once every 60 seconds.
decomposes: OPS-MONITOR-001
end requirement

requirement SENSOR-LEVEL-001
title: Measure water level
statement:
  The level-sensing unit shall provide a water-level measurement with each station sample.
decomposes: SYS-MONITOR-SAMPLE-001
end requirement

requirement SENSOR-WEATHER-001
title: Measure precipitation
statement:
  The weather-sensing unit shall provide accumulated precipitation with each station sample.
decomposes: SYS-MONITOR-SAMPLE-001
end requirement

requirement SYS-MONITOR-QUALIFY-001
title: Qualify sampled data
statement:
  Each station shall identify sampled values that are unavailable, stale, or outside configured physical limits.
decomposes: OPS-MONITOR-001
end requirement

requirement EDGE-RANGE-001
title: Check physical limits
statement:
  The station processor shall compare each sampled value with its configured physical limits.
decomposes: SYS-MONITOR-QUALIFY-001
end requirement

requirement EDGE-STALE-001
title: Detect stale samples
statement:
  The station processor shall mark a sensor value stale when no new sample is available for three sampling periods.
decomposes: SYS-MONITOR-QUALIFY-001
end requirement

requirement SYS-MONITOR-PUBLISH-001
title: Publish station status
statement:
  The service shall make the latest qualified sample and station status available within 90 seconds of acquisition.
decomposes: OPS-MONITOR-001
end requirement

requirement GATEWAY-INGEST-001
title: Ingest station samples
statement:
  The gateway shall ingest qualified samples from every configured station.
decomposes: SYS-MONITOR-PUBLISH-001
end requirement

requirement API-STATUS-001
title: Serve current status
statement:
  The status interface shall return the latest qualified sample and its acquisition time for a requested station.
decomposes: SYS-MONITOR-PUBLISH-001
end requirement
